{
  "dom_id": "step-q345269",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A series RCL circuit has a source electromotive force (EMF) of $9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistance of $18\\,Ω,$ a capacitance of $0.002\\,\\text{F},$ and an inductance of $L=9\\,\\text{H}.$ Find the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ (in amperes) in the circuit at time $t$ (in seconds).\n\n*Hint: The voltage drop ${V}_{C}$ across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C},$ where $C$ is the capacitance measured in Farads.*",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
